sequenceDiagram
    participant B as Booking service
    participant P as Payment service
    participant D as Payments DB
    participant S as PSP adapter
    participant R as Pending resolver
    B->>P: authorize 4,200 THB, Idempotency-Key = booking_id:1
    P->>D: insert payment CREATED and idempotency row in one transaction
    P->>D: insert attempt 1 with request body
    P->>S: create payment intent, Idempotency-Key forwarded to PSP
    S--xP: timeout after 8 s
    P->>D: attempt 1 = TIMEOUT, payment = PENDING_PSP
    P-->>B: 202 PENDING, poll or wait for event
    R->>P: pick PENDING_PSP older than 30 s
    P->>S: get payment intent by our idempotency key
    S-->>P: status = requires_capture, amount 4,200
    P->>D: payment = AUTHORIZED, ledger entries, outbox PaymentAuthorized, one transaction
    P-->>B: PaymentAuthorized event via Kafka
    Note over P,S: A timeout is never treated as failure and never retried blind. The PSP is asked what happened first.
